I am about to go out of the shop.
Just then, I see a cotton shirt.
This shirt is very bright and beautiful.
It has a very good design on it.
I like it a lot.
But there is a lot of humidity in Mumbai today.
I am very tired from the heat.
I ask the shopkeeper, "Bhaiya, how much is this shirt?"
He says, "Madam, it is for five hundred rupees."
I say, "Okay, please pack this too."
I do not try the shirt on.
I just want to go back to my flat quickly.
Bhaiya packs the shirt.
He gives me the bag and a paper receipt.
"Madam, this is your receipt," he says.
"Thank you bhaiya," I say.
I keep the receipt safely in my bag.
I come out of the shop.
I take the bus and go back to my flat.
